      <h2><a href="/unity/">Unity of thought</a></h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <p>There is an ability I call <em>unity of thought</em>, for a lack of a better word, which is essential for acquiring intelligence/wisdom. It is the ability to connect each new idea/view that you have, with all the other ideas/views in your mind, to make it compatible with those. And to drop the ideas and views that aren’t compatible.</p>

<p>(it is called <em>holding</em> a view for a reason — it takes effort and you cannot do it with too many of those.)</p>

<p>Unifying your thoughts sets your mind free, but it requires commitment.</p>

<p>It requires that you remain consistent in your thoughts and view, even in contexts where this is not beneficial to you.</p>

<p>It requires you to reject the ideas that your brain wants you to reject.</p>

<p>No compromise.</p>

<p>Trying to balance a different set of views and ideas, depending on the situation, will make you dumb and will mess up your mental health…</p>

      </div>

